## Introduction or Why building functional e-commerce platforms for toddlers can be a thing

‘Toddler’ and ‘e-commerce’ are two words that I didn’t expect to be combining this year, but here we are in this new AI world, and I’m finding that with the latest agents and a little thought on how to harness them, that I'm building plenty of unexpected, but really cool, projects.

The goal for this one was to create a fun toy, while also learning more about e-commerce particularly the Stripe Payments APIs. I wanted to replicate a point of sale terminal, with an iPad app, a linked barcode scanner and Stripe card reader. The app would show a checkout screen and I would place QR code stickers on toys. Each toy could then be scanned and payment made with a special Stripe test credit card.

This was to be my most ambitious side-project yet, for a few reasons:

1. **It involved hardware.** Hardware is fun but in the past I've found it so time consuming to utilize, with long iteration and debug cycles, that any new kit I've bought has just gathered dust. Agents let me cut through a lot of the frustration and it was a lot of fun. Here's what we had to play with:

