Underneath this workflow, we've got an e-commerce stack:

<div class="mermaid-container">

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'dark'}}%%
graph TD
    subgraph ClientDevices [Client Devices and Peripherals - Used In Store]
        iPadApp["iPad POS App<br/>Swift / iOS"]
        BarcodeScanner["Tera Mini Barcode Scanner<br/>Bluetooth HID Mode"]
        StripeReader["Stripe Reader M2<br/>Bluetooth BLE Mode"]
    end

    subgraph ExternalServices [External Integrations]
        StripeAPI["Stripe API<br/>Terminal and Payments"]
        AppAttest["Apple App Attest Service<br/>Device Verification"]
    end

    subgraph EdgeBackend [Cloudflare Workers Edge Platform]
        RustWorker["Payments and Admin API Worker<br/>Rust / Wasm"]
        subgraph CloudflareStorage [Cloudflare Storage]
            D1Db["D1 Relational DB<br/>SQLite Transactions"]
            KVStore["KV Namespace<br/>Inventory Data"]
        end
    end

    subgraph AdminControl [Admin Portal]
        AdminUI["Admin Website in Browser<br/>www.fintechnick.com"]
        AveryPrinter["Avery Label Printer<br/>AirPrint from Browser"]
    end

    BarcodeScanner -->|Bluetooth HID / Keystrokes| iPadApp
    StripeReader <-->|Bluetooth BLE / Stripe Terminal SDK| iPadApp
    iPadApp <-->|HTTPS REST / App Attest Signed| RustWorker
    AdminUI -->|Store inventory updates via HTTPS REST / X-Admin-API-Key| RustWorker

    RustWorker <-->|Cloudflare Binding| D1Db
    RustWorker <-->|Cloudflare Binding| KVStore

    RustWorker <-->|HTTPS / REST API| StripeAPI
    RustWorker -->|HTTPS / Validation Requests| AppAttest
    AdminUI -->|Browser Render / CSS @media print| AveryPrinter
    AveryPrinter -.->|Printed QR labels scanned in store| BarcodeScanner
```

</div>

There's three main pieces:

1. **Swift iPad app** that the scanner connects to in Bluetooth keyboard-wedge mode, meaning it mimics a keyboard, while the M2 scanner integrates through the [Stripe Terminal SDK](https://docs.stripe.com/terminal) and every request is signed with Apple App Attest so only my iPad can talk to the backend.

2. **Rust worker on Cloudflare** that the iPad communicates with[^2]. The worker issues Stripe Terminal tokens that lets the Stripe Terminal SDK connect to the card reader, creates and captures `card_present` [PaymentIntents](https://docs.stripe.com/api/payment_intents) that represent the payment lifecycle, and keeps photos and prices of inventory in Cloudflare's key-value storage [KV](https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/) with a transaction log in Cloudflare's Serverless SQL (SQLite) [D1](https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/).

3. **Admin website** for inventory photo upload, pricing, QR generation, label printing, and a bit of analytics.

